    overwrite the rights specifications in &lt;<a
            href="https://lido-schema.org/schema/latest/lido.html#recordRights">lido:recordRights</a>&gt;.</p>
            <h4 data-number="4.4.2.3" id="resource"><span
            class="header-section-number">4.4.2.3</span> Resource</h4>
            <p>The <a
            href="http://lido-schema.org/schema/latest/lido.html#resourceWrap"><strong>Resource
            Wrapper</strong></a> contains information about the digital
            resource or resources that serve as a surrogate for the
            object or work. Typically this consists of one or more
            digital representations such as digital images, video or
            audio files, or 3D models for online access. Information
            includes the type of the resource and its digital format, as
            well as its source and rights. Note that the resource
            element does not apply to items that are considered
            objects/works in their own right, but only to surrogates of
            such. The rights associated with the resource are documented
            in &lt;<a
            href="https://lido-schema.org/schema/latest/lido.html#rightsResource">lido:rightsResource</a>&gt;.</p>
            <blockquote>
            <p>For further information about metadata see NISO (2017):
            <a
            href="https://www.niso.org/publications/understanding-metadata-2017">Understanding
            Metadata: What is Metadata, and What is it For?: A
            Primer</a></p>
            </blockquote>
            <h2 data-number="4.5" id="element-structure"><span
            class="header-section-number">4.5</span> Element
            structure</h2>
            <p>Some content elements in LIDO follow a fixed structural
            pattern: A LIDO
            <abbr title="In LIDO a repeatable structural element">set</abbr>,
            e.g., &lt;<a href="">lido:subjectActor</a>&gt;, comprises a
            <abbr title="In LIDO a free-text element for human-readable descriptions">display
            element</abbr> followed by elements holding indexing
            information. This structure applies particularly to named
            entities for which an identifier may be used, such as actor,
            event, object, and place (see <a
            href="https://lido-schema.org/schema/latest/lido.html#identifierComplexType"><em>identifierComplexType</em></a>).
            This pattern is also followed for, e.g., collection
            information, descriptions of materials and techniques, or
            measurements. For more information on display and index
            elements see section <a
            href="#display-and-index-elements"><em>4.3.3 Display and
            index elements</em></a>.</p>
            <h3 data-number="4.5.1"
            id="overview-of-the-structure-and-the-elements"><span
            class="header-section-number">4.5.1</span> Overview of the
            structure and the elements</h3>
            <p>The following figure shows the element structure, and an
            example for the description of an actor as subject of the
            described object or work. The sequence of the sub-elements
            of &lt;<a
            href="https://lido-schema.org/schema/latest/lido.html#actor_actorSetComplexType">lido:actor</a>&gt;
            is determined by the LIDO specification for <a
            href="https://lido-schema.org/schema/latest/lido.html#actorComplexType"><em>actorComplexType</em></a>.</p>
            <figure>
            <img src="img/figure_element-structure.jpg"
            alt="Figure 9: Element structure for a named entity" />
            <figcaption aria-hidden="true">Figure 9: Element structure
            for a named entity</figcaption>
            </figure>
            <p><strong>Example:</strong> The following XML code snippet
            includes display and index elements to record identifying
            information about a person and its “<a
            href="http://terminology.lido-schema.org/lido01027">Cultural
            affiliation</a>” as a type for &lt;<a
            href="https://lido-schema.org/schema/latest/lido.html#nationalityActor">lido:nationalityActor</a>&gt;.</p>
            <div class="sourceCode" id="cb19"><pre
            class="sourceCode xml"><code class="sourceCode xml"><span id="cb19-1"><a href="#cb19-1" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a>&lt;<span class="kw">lido:subjectActor</span>&gt;</span>
<span id="cb19-2"><a href="#cb19-2" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a>    &lt;<span class="kw">lido:displayActor</span><span class="ot"> xml:lang=</span><span class="st">&quot;{...}&quot;</span>&gt;</span>
<span id="cb19-3"><a href="#cb19-3" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a>        [...]</span>
<span id="cb19-4"><a href="#cb19-4" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a>    &lt;/<span class="kw">lido:displayActor</span>&gt;</span>
<span id="cb19-5"><a href="#cb19-5" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a>    <span class="co">&lt;!-- Person --&gt;</span></span>
<span id="cb19-6"><a href="#cb19-6" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a>    &lt;<span class="kw">lido:actor</span></span>
<span id="cb19-7"><a href="#cb19-7" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a><span class="ot">        lido:type=</span><span class="st">&quot;http://terminology.lido-schema.org/lido00163&quot;</span>&gt;</span>
<span id="cb19-8"><a href="#cb19-8" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a>        &lt;<span class="kw">lido:actorID</span><span class="ot"> lido:type=</span><span class="st">&quot;{...}&quot;</span>&gt;</span>
<span id="cb19-9"><a href="#cb19-9" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a>            [...]</span>
<span id="cb19-10"><a href="#cb19-10" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a>        &lt;/<span class="kw">lido:actorID</span>&gt;</span>
<span id="cb19-11"><a href="#cb19-11" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a>        &lt;<span class="kw">lido:nameActorSet</span>&gt;</span>
<span id="cb19-12"><a href="#cb19-12" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a>            <span class="co">&lt;!-- Preferred name --&gt;</span></span>
<span id="cb19-13"><a href="#cb19-13" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a>            &lt;<span class="kw">lido:appellationValue</span></span>
<span id="cb19-14"><a href="#cb19-14" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a><span class="ot">                lido:pref=</span><span class="st">&quot;http://terminology.lido-schema.org/lido00169&quot;</span></span>
<span id="cb19-15"><a href="#cb19-15" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a><span class="ot">                xml:lang=</span><span class="st">&quot;{...}&quot;</span>&gt;</span>
<span id="cb19-16"><a href="#cb19-16" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a>                [...]</span>
<span id="cb19-17"><a href="#cb19-17" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a>            &lt;/<span class="kw">lido:appellationValue</span>&gt;</span>
<span id="cb19-18"><a href="#cb19-18" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a>        &lt;/<span class="kw">lido:nameActorSet</span>&gt;</span>
<span id="cb19-19"><a href="#cb19-19" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a>        <span class="co">&lt;!-- Cultural affiliation --&gt;</span></span>
<span id="cb19-20"><a href="#cb19-20" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a>        &lt;<span class="kw">lido:nationalityActor</span></span>
<span id="cb19-21"><a href="#cb19-21" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a><span class="ot">            lido:type=</span><span class="st">&quot;http://terminology.lido-schema.org/lido01027&quot;</span>&gt;</span>
<span id="cb19-22"><a href="#cb19-22" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a>            &lt;<span class="kw">skos:Concept</span><span class="ot"> rdf:about=</span><span class="st">&quot;{...}&quot;</span>&gt;&lt;/<span class="kw">skos:Concept</span>&gt;</span>
<span id="cb19-23"><a href="#cb19-23" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a>        &lt;/<span class="kw">lido:nationalityActor</span>&gt;</span>
<span id="cb19-24"><a href="#cb19-24" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a>    &lt;/<span class="kw">lido:actor</span>&gt;</span>
<span id="cb19-2